4. Modifications made in this package relative to `stockfish` 1.8.1
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Renamed the package to `stockfish_engine_flutter` (library entry point is
  `package:stockfish_engine_flutter/stockfish_engine_flutter.dart`), version
  0.1.0, new repository, Dart 3 SDK constraint.
* Android: Stockfish is no longer loaded as a JNI/FFI shared library
  (`libstockfish.so`). It is built as an executable named `libstockfish_bin.so`
  (android/CMakeLists.txt, `add_executable`), started from `nativeLibraryDir`
  with `Process.start` and driven over stdin/stdout. `ios/FlutterStockfish/ffi.cpp`
  is no longer compiled for Android.
* Android: added `android:extractNativeLibs="true"` to the plugin manifest and
  a `nativeLibraryDir` method channel (StockfishPlugin.java).
* Android: CMake now reads the NNUE file names from `evaluate.h`, downloads
  missing networks and verifies their SHA-256 prefix (the previous CMake file
  downloaded two obsolete network names that were never used).
* Stockfish src/nnue/network.cpp: when STOCKFISH_EXTERNAL_NETS is defined
  (Android builds only) the networks are referenced with INCBIN_EXTERN instead
  of being embedded; they are embedded once in android/stockfish_nets.cpp
  (libstockfish_nets.so). Without the macro the file behaves as before.
* Android: arm64-v8a release builds ship an additional engine executable
  without dot-product instructions (libstockfish_bin_compat.so), selected at
  runtime from /proc/cpuinfo.
* iOS: removed -flto=full and the dot-product flags from the Release build.
* iOS: podspec license corrected from MIT to GPL-3.0, authors/homepage updated,
  and the nnue download script phases updated to the networks that
  `evaluate.h` actually requires (nn-7bf13f9655c8, nn-47fc8b7fff06). The FFI
  path itself is unchanged. The podspec is now `stockfish_engine_flutter.podspec`.
* macOS (dev path): the bundled prebuilt-binary asset mechanism was removed;
  the engine is built from the package sources (networks fetched with curl).
* Dart: `Stockfish` selects the process backend on Android and macOS and the
  FFI backend on iOS; the public API (state, stdin setter, stdout stream,
  dispose, stockfishAsync) is unchanged.
* Removed build artifacts and the prebuilt macOS binary from the tree.
